      },
      "message": "feat(contour): a picked start point with tabs on closed 2D contours\n\nA closed 2D Contour with tabs now takes a user start point. On the\npicked ring the tab windows are measured from the pick: the same count,\nwidth and spacing, the last tab ends on the seam, so every level, the\ntabbed ones too, enters at the pick. The picked start's lead-in law runs\non the first window only. A ring without a pick keeps the automatic tab\nlayout move for move. The exit point with tabs stays refused by name.\n\nRefs #1473\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
